A||N||5||gkozlov||Can't shift into 5th or reverse-PLEASE HELP!||||1||
Z||000000||gkozlov||04-27-2001||08:47 PM||||My buddy has a 87 GT that just won't shift into 5th gear or reverse.  The only way to get it to shift into the far right gears is to assist him at the tranny see pic "3".  Does shifter cable "1" have to be replaced or is tranny work in order, how do I find out?  Any help would be appreciated.  Thanks in advance.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ext.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/int.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">     <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A><BR>MSN MESSENGER: wkozlov@hotmail.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||04-27-2001||09:02 PM||||your shift SELECT cable is out of adjustment - correct it by adjusting it on the bracket where it meets the transmission<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||04-27-2001||09:02 PM||||Your select cable could be broken. 1st and 2nd push the cable so even if its broken it will still give you 1 and 2. Fifth and reverse pull on it. When you install a replacement make sure you route it as far away from the exhaust as possible.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR><p>[This message has been edited by PJ (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||gkozlov||04-27-2001||10:00 PM||||How do we go about adjusting this cable if not broken? <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">     <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A><BR>MSN MESSENGER: wkozlov@hotmail.com||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tryxalon||04-27-2001||10:06 PM||||The connection at the Tranny is in a slot or notch not a single hole so you can adjust the cable. <P>To test it: move the selector on the tranny and see if it moves the shift lever in the car. Better yet, loosen the connection on the tranny selector and push,pull on the cable. <P>If you can move the shifter both right and left from the transmission, - okay, you can adjust it. .. see your shop manual (or chiltons or Haynes) for the procedure. <P>IF you cannot move the shifter both ways -- yep you have a broken cable and it MUST be replaced. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||gkozlov||04-28-2001||09:20 PM||||Thanks to all that replied. We have determined that it is the cables not the tranny.  He is going to buy a new one.  Once again thanks.  The car is going up for sale. Im going to post it in the appropriate section.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">     <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A><BR>MSN MESSENGER: wkozlov@hotmail.com||||reg||1
